---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { site } from "../site";
---

<Layout title="Privacy Policy" description="Blanky collects no data. Here is exactly what it stores, and where.">
  <div class="container page">
    <header class="page-header">
      <h1 class="display">Privacy Policy</h1>
      <p class="lede">Short version: Blanky collects nothing. Its only connection is an update check with GitHub.</p>
    </header>
    <div class="prose">
      <h2>The app</h2>
      <p>
        Blanky has no accounts, analytics, ads or crash reporting. Everything it stores stays on your PC in{" "}
        <code>%LOCALAPPDATA%\Blanky</code>:
      </p>
      <ul>
        <li>your settings, presets and favorites (JSON files);</li>
        <li>copies of sounds you import, and preset artwork;</li>
        <li>a small log file, <code>blanky.log</code>, rewritten at each launch, that records audio device events to help fix bugs. It never leaves your PC unless you attach it to a bug report yourself.</li>
      </ul>
      <p>Deleting that folder removes everything Blanky has stored.</p>

      <h2>Updates</h2>
      <p>
        When it starts and every few hours while it runs, Blanky asks GitHub whether a newer version has been released,
        and if so downloads it from GitHub. These are ordinary web requests to GitHub's servers: they include your IP
        address, as every web request does, and nothing about you or how you use Blanky. GitHub handles them under{" "}
        <a href="https://docs.github.com/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">its privacy statement</a>.
      </p>
      <p>The app itself is installed in <code>%LOCALAPPDATA%\Blanky.App</code>. Uninstalling removes it and leaves your data in place.</p>

      <h2>This website</h2>
      <p>
        This site is hosted on GitHub Pages and uses no cookies, analytics or trackers. GitHub may keep standard server
        logs; see <a href="https://docs.github.com/site-policy/privacy-policies/github-general-privacy-statement">GitHub's privacy statement</a>.
        Links to GitHub, Buy Me a Coffee and other sites are covered by their own policies.
      </p>

      <h2>Questions</h2>
      <p>Open an issue on <a href={site.issues}>GitHub</a>.</p>
      <p>Last updated: October 28, 2026.</p>
    </div>
  </div>
</Layout>
